--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
take_view\.h line 348: C\+\+ front-end dropped the body
--
libc++'s views::take(n) (take_view.h:348) returns
`__range_adaptor_closure_t(std::__bind_back(*this, std::forward<_Np>(__n)))';
in __bind_back_op::operator()'s noexcept and trailing return types
(bind_back.h:60) the front end reports "template 'forward' not found" and
drops take's call operator (cpp20_views_take_call_crash).  cvise
reduction running in /tmp/r163/red/kb_U6.  clang++ 18 with libc++ accepts
the program.  Pre-existing (fails on bin52).
Fixed (round 163v): the suppressed error was "found no match for symbol
'forward_as_tuple'" for `decltype(forward_as_tuple(__args...))' in
__bind_back's trailing return type: guess_function_template_args took
`_Args' as an empty pack because an older, empty pack of another template
had the same short name ([basic.scope.temp]/2: the innermost declaration is
the one named).  The program still drops the __tuple_impl and tuple
constructors (tuple:469/488/713; cpp20_libcxx_header_drops/
test_functional.desc), which this test does not check.
